# AbroBot CRM — routing during the frontend takeover.
#
# Two apps share this domain:
#   legacy.html  → the original bundle (index-Bw0EU57x.js). Still owns the
#                  marketing, pricing, trial and credit flows — i.e. the money.
#   index.html   → the new app (app/dist). Owns the CRM itself.
#
# Order matters: Cloudflare Pages applies the FIRST matching rule, so every
# legacy route must appear above the catch-all.
#
# Static files (pricing.html, contact-us.html, terms-and-conditions.html,
# refund-and-cancellation-policy.html, product.html) are served directly and
# need no rule — real files always win over the fallback.
#
# To hand a route to the new app, delete its line here and redeploy.
# To hand one back, add it. That is the whole cutover mechanism.

# ── still served by the legacy bundle ────────────────────────────────────────
/get            /legacy.html   200
/onboarding     /legacy.html   200
/myday          /legacy.html   200
/priority       /legacy.html   200
/compose        /legacy.html   200
/analytics      /legacy.html   200
/leaderboard    /legacy.html   200
/super          /legacy.html   200

# ── everything else: the new app ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/*              /index.html    200
